WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.450
Eight rules come out of that.

2
00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:04.755
A policy in detection, or
disabled, is a finding,

3
00:00:04.755 --> 00:00:07.538
and so is body inspection switched off.

4
00:00:07.538 --> 00:00:13.000
A missing or older rule set, no bot
protection, and no rate limit are warnings.

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.426
An internet-facing gateway or Front Door
profile with no WAF at all is a finding,

6
00:00:18.426 --> 00:00:22.350
and so is one that sends no
logs to the platform workspace.

7
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.074
And a Front Door policy that
isn't Premium is information:

8
00:00:26.074 --> 00:00:27.975
it can't use managed rule sets.

9
00:00:27.975 --> 00:00:31.541
Coverage is the endpoints
behind a WAF in prevention

10
00:00:31.541 --> 00:00:35.188
over all internet-facing
endpoints, the guide's metric.

11
00:00:35.188 --> 00:00:38.690
A gateway with only a private
frontend isn't counted.
